.TH AGENT-HOOK-TELEMETRY 1 "2026-11-11" "agentguard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-hook-telemetry \- record an agent hook event in the audit trail
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-hook-telemetry
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-hook-telemetry
reads any hook JSON payload from standard input and records its complete
content (re-serialized compactly; non-JSON input is kept as text) as an
.B event
record in the session's audit directory under
.IR ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/agentguard/telemetry/sessions/ .
It always prints an empty JSON response and exits 0: it never blocks, warns,
or injects context, so it is safe to register beside any guard hook.
.PP
AgentGuard's native integrations register it for every wired event with a
match-all tool matcher, so prompts, tool inputs, tool outputs, and lifecycle
events are captured, including tools no guard inspects. The wired events per
runtime are listed in
.IR docs/telemetry.md .
Every other
.B agent-hook-*
entry point writes a companion
.B hook
record with its decision (exit status, block and warning messages, injected
context) but not the payload.
.PP
When the payload looks like a session start, a background pass deletes
sessions idle for longer than
.B AGENTGUARD_TELEMETRY_RETENTION_DAYS
days.
.PP
A
.B StopFailure
or
.B Interrupt
event for the foreground turn ends it without a Stop callback, and only this
hook is wired to those events, so it also clears the agent's busy tmux pane
mark with
.BR "term-pane-mark clear busy" ,
whether or not recording is enabled.
A subagent's event (one carrying
.BR agent_id )
and an
.B Interrupt
whose
.B reason
is
.B superseded
(sent after the steering prompt that replaced the turn) leave the mark set.
After the busy clear, a foreground
.B StopFailure
rings
.B term-notify-sound
with attention kind
.B blocked
when it wins the prompt cycle's single bell (the one a ringing
.BR agent-hook-stop (1)
holds) and records the session's
.I attention-sticky
flag. A blocked mark stays until the next prompt or the end of the session.
Any other foreground turn end clears a waiting or blocked mark with
.BR "term-pane-mark clear pending \-\-if sticky" .
.PP
Waiting attention (see
.BR agent-hook-notification (1))
ends with the agent's next activity. A
.B PreToolUse
event only tests whether the flag file exists, which starts no process while
nothing waits; when it exists and the tool's actor (the root agent, or the
child routed by the payload's
.B agent_id
or Muse's child session) raised it, or the flag accepts any actor, the hook clears it with
.BR "term-pane-mark clear pending \-\-if waiting" .
A child's
.B SubagentStop
or
.B StopFailure
does the same for a waiting mark that child raised. The flag is removed before
the mark is cleared. A release of
.B term-pane-mark
that rejects
.B \-\-if
only loses the flag; the hook never falls back to a plain clear, which would
erase unseen attention. Gemini CLI reports tools as
.BR BeforeTool ,
which this hook does not observe, so its waiting mark lasts until the turn
ends.
.PP
For Claude, each subagent or teammate turn keeps the pane busy from its
.B SubagentStart
to its
.B SubagentStop
or a
.B StopFailure
carrying its
.BR agent_id ,
even after the parent turn ends. A Claude
.B Notification
whose
.B notification_type
is
.B idle_prompt
means the parent and every child agent are idle, so it clears the mark and
retires children whose Stop never arrived.
The team state also records each child's latest start time, which hook
extensions read through
.BR _hook_child_working .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_TELEMETRY
Set to 0, false, no, or off to disable recording.
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_TELEMETRY_DIR
Absolute path of the telemetry root; relative values are ignored.
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_TELEMETRY_RETENTION_DAYS
Retention window in days (default 90); 0 keeps every session.
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_TELEMETRY_MAX_PAYLOAD_CHARS
Payload length above which only a prefix is kept (default 8388608).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/agentguard/telemetry/sessions/AGENT/SESSION/*.json
One JSON record per hook invocation, owner-only. The schema is documented in
.I docs/telemetry.md
in the AgentGuard checkout.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Always 0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agent-hook-notification (1),
.BR agentguard-telemetry (1),
.BR term-notify-sound (1),
.BR term-pane-mark (1)
